From: Bernhard Rosenkränzer <bero@lindev.ch>
Subject: Build fusestore as a static library

os links fusestore, and the object-store tools link it too. With
BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON, fusestore becomes libfusestore.so with an
unversioned SONAME, and nothing installs that library. The daemons
then require a file cooker does not ship. fusestore is internal.

diff -up a/src/os/CMakeLists.txt b/src/os/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/src/os/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/os/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@ if(WITH_BLUESTORE)
 endif()
 
 if(WITH_FUSE)
-  add_library(fusestore
+  add_library(fusestore STATIC
     FuseStore.cc)
   target_link_libraries(fusestore
     PRIVATE FUSE::FUSE)
